  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Kia Forte?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. Query the fuel signals in the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. To catch refuels, request segments with the refuel mechanism, which detects where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Kia Forte with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Kia Forte?",
      "a": "A DIMO device provides idling detection. Call the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling mechanism, which finds contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range. You can tune the idle ceiling with maxIdleRpm, which defaults to 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect harsh braking on a Kia Forte?",
      "a": "The harsh braking event is listed for the DIMO LTE R1 device. Create a webhook in the Vehicle Triggers API on the events service with the metricName behavior.harshBraking, then subscribe the vehicle to it."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Kia Forte mileage?",
      "a": "A DIMO device reports the odometer signal. To get verifiable proof, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the resulting credential through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a Kia Forte vehicle data API through a DIMO device, covering model years 2017 and newer. Coverage for this model is tested rather than expected, and the record notes no gaps. Developers read signals through the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT after the owner shares the vehicle with their Developer License. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance."
